 # Combat model
 
+## Dual styles prototype v12 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User policy (high):** fix the Close offhand blinking during Glide/Superglide. In Ranged,
+Sora stays in Final idle while the weapons retain their spin; up to three spins form a
+normal finite combo, extended by combo abilities. The air version uses the same idle and
+spin while holding Sora's height for that combo.
+
+### Close native glide draw refresh
+
+**Evidence and confidence:** the user reports v11 blinking; no new log or recording was
+supplied. Source inspection shows LEFT is published only by pose callbacks, and a world
+WeaponPose older than one physics frame is rejected by the draw. Normal-body admission
+also used only body callbacks. A static/native glide can therefore lose the duplicate
+between body rebuilds. The complete native bone array's finiteness also gated a cosmetic
+attachment that only needs its left hand. These are source-confirmed visibility gaps;
+actual live cause and resolution need the user's next game test.
+
+The existing queue hook now recognizes a draw only for the exact live field actor's exact
+SORA_INSTANCE and verified 293-bone body; that draw refreshes normal-body admission.
+Before the Close native state-21 duplicate draw, read its current active matrix array's
+left hand, verify the binding and finite, nonsingular hand within 300 units of the actor,
+and rebuild the duplicate from its validated hand-local NativeAttachment calibration.
+Actor/model/matrix/weapon/generation changes reject that calibration. No old world-space
+pose is renewed and no missed-frame geometry is carried forward. The one-frame expiry
+rule is retained for attack and other pose consumers. No trail/contact is started here.
+The native primary/body draw and temporary weapon-matrix restoration stay unchanged.
+Both Glide variants remain held cosmetic poses with no glide damage.
+
+### Independent Final idle body and ground-spin weapons
+
+The Ranged attack controller still owns only the sanitized physical action. RigAnim first
+samples/unroots Final ground Aero-family motion 65 for both weapons. It then replaces only
+its body-bone array with Final combat IDLE 0 evaluated on a separate LoopClock, using the
+existing native animation time and idle_speed. The idle's own root is removed; the two
+weapon arrays are preserved verbatim. The resulting body signature and both weapons are
+published together, so the offhand lookup and native retargeting consume the same mixed
+pose. Original cast/body data is never stepped as a spell/controller. Missing/invalid idle
+retires the attack instead of showing the casting gesture. Admission now requires idle
+and ground-spin clips; aerial cast 67 remains available to native spells but is no longer
+needed or selected by Attack. The same physical spin 65 is used for all four ground/air
+ordinary/finisher rows; the row's true air flag still selects native air contact semantics.
+
+### Finite press count and aerial hold
+
+Character has an explicit host combo_on_miss option, false by default. Only this Ranged
+adapter enables it. Valid Attack presses in the existing last-quarter chain window count
+on through whiffs without setting any Combo Master ability/equipped/save bit or registering
+a fabricated hit. Native/default and Close controllers retain the previous hit policy.
+The existing counter provides a three-slot base, Combo Plus on ground, Air Combo Plus in
+air, a finite final finisher, and no automatic repeats from holding a button alone. Nothing
+runs a spell-to-attack follow-up. The new host policy changes no ATKP power or hit records.
+
