 # Combat model
 
+## Dual styles prototype v13 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User policy (high):** rename Close to Style: Dual A and Ranged to Style: Dual B.
+Dual B's basic combo uses Final's first three attacks like Dual A's Valor combo;
+Dodge Roll uses Master's aerial dodge; Guard uses the previous basic blade spin.
+Previously requested passive ability/equipped-weapon/exclusivity rules remain.
+
+### Names and base combos
+
+Only the displayed names/help change. IDs 126/125, 0 AP, learned/equipped bytes and
+exclusive equip behavior stay identical, so this update migrates no inventory or save
+layout. Internal Close/Ranged identifiers remain to avoid changing unrelated routing.
+
+**Source/confidence:** existing kh2-data Final PTYA loader, base-row filter and Character
+selector (high for source behavior). Dual B clones Final's real base ground/air rows,
+removing ability rows, ground-hop rows and the explicit Guard row. It admits only rows
+with actual per-weapon hit windows and available rig motions, then fixes sub references
+before adding Guard. It uses the ordinary three-slot ground/air cap, finite finisher and
+native Combo Plus/Air Combo Plus. It preserves v12's explicit press-counted whiff policy
+without setting Combo Master. No guessed chronological motion-number list is substituted
+for the donor selector. Actual installed Final PTYA/motions are loaded at runtime; no
+Final bank was supplied for local appearance/chronological verification.
+
+Final's actual body and melee root tracks now play during those attacks. Clear donor
+events and spell/body/defensive/command-offer windows; keep authored melee timing and
+movement windows. No old idle-body override or blanket aerial NoGravity is applied to
+basic combos. Both styles use the existing native whole-lane attack-ability priority:
+equipped KH1 action attacks retain their native combo and cosmetic offhand. Combo
+Plus/Air Combo Plus alone do not force a native lane. Physical limits remain blocked in B.
+
+### Guard and Dodge Roll
+
+**Source/confidence:** the already verified native control-hook Guard/Roll flags,
+command word, stats threshold and direction magnitude (high, no new address). Require
+native Guard flag 0x10 or Dodge Roll flag 0x20 respectively, free ground state 0, fresh
+Square command, native can-act, no chosen command/jump/shortcut/menu/scene/deep-water
+priority. When both abilities are equipped, native threshold versus tilt chooses exactly
+one action. Consume that selection once before forwarding original control once.
+
+Dual B's selected Guard runs one sanitized spin 65 from v12 with Final looping idle
+body 0 and unchanged spinning weapon tracks. Retain only weapon contacts and the local
+NoGravity window; remove combo/follow-up/cast events and every donor defensive window.
+No Aero spell/effect/projectile, MP cost or automatic Attack chain is created. Dual A
+retains its existing Valor rising Guard action. Guard itself is still required.
+
+Master loads via the existing data-only visual loader for Dual B's selected ground
+Dodge Roll. **Source/confidence:** existing Master motion 202/AERIAL_DODGE mapping,
+growth[0] aerial-dodge height/speed and Character action implementation (high for source,
+live timing/appearance unverified). Require two weapon tracks, available bounded clip
+and finite bounded movement data. The host starts that one AerialDodge action from the
+ground without granting growth, Guard, Dodge Roll or any other native ability. Keep
+authored root/guard windows, strip hitboxes, invulnerability and all events. Master casts,
+scripts and effect archives are never started. A missing donor retains native Dodge Roll.
+This replaces ground Dodge Roll input; it adds no airborne action input.
+
+The active action selects its correct controller/rig/battle data and hand attachment:
+Final for basic combos/Guard, Master for Dodge Roll. Basic Attack cannot execute under
+the defensive replacements. A native action-running damage request 0x48..0x51 cancels
+their ownership even if KH1 keeps state 0. Existing damage/death/scenes, native commands,
+binding/weapon/map/style changes and timeout/freshness guards still retire ownership.
+Actual displayed Final blade geometry is keyed by the current motion rather than only
+spin 65/67; the same one-frame binding/phase/translation bounds and native contact path
+apply to all admitted combo motions. No direct HP writes or new hook addresses.
+
+### Validation and limits
+
+Portable tests use synthetic donor fixtures to exercise three-slot and extended ground/
+air Final selectors, single Guard/no follow-up, actual melee roots, ability/sub-row
+filtering, exclusive native Guard/Roll priority, native damage classification and one
+Master launch/end with invalid-data rejection and no ability grant. Retained tests cover
+names/save exclusivity, blade geometry, glides, casts and the original controller policy.
+All 327 tests passed across 18 suites, including 98 Dual Wield tests. Windows x64 release
+cross-build passed; PE and package receipts accompany the deliverable. No live game run,
+new log/recording or installed Final/Master donor bank is available in this session.
+
