@@ -1,5 +1,97 @@
 # Combat model
 
+## Dual styles prototype v14 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User policy (high):** Dual A Superglide uses Valor's air-combo finisher. Remove the
+voice over Dual B Guard; replace B Dodge Roll with a moving version of that same spin.
+Use KH2 magic animations with B. All existing passive-style/equipped-weapon rules remain.
+
+### Dual A Superglide
+
+**Source/confidence:** runtime Valor PTYA base-row flags, existing combo/clip loaders,
+visual retargeting and native subtype guard (high for code behavior, live appearance
+unverified). Read a kind-3, ability-free aerial finisher row with bounded clip length and
+actual weapon hit windows; prefer the base row 8 if present, otherwise the first admitted
+base finisher. Verify its real rig motion. No fixed guessed motion number is selected.
+
+Only A's Superglide now selects Valor as its visual donor and the admitted finisher motion.
+The existing continuous animation clock repeats it while native Superglide remains active.
+Sample body/both weapons together and remove cumulative root travel, so KH1 still owns
+position, speed, turning, floor collision, ability gates and button-release retirement.
+The finisher Character is never stepped; its hit windows/events/voices/trails do not run.
+No A glide damage is added. A regular Glide keeps the native held pose/live-hand refresh.
