 # Combat model
 
+## Dual styles prototype v15 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User report/policy (high):** B still plays native Dodge Roll. A must execute the aerial
+finisher instead of keeping Superglide's movement. B needs actual KH2 spell effects,
+not only KH2 casting animations. No current game log/recording was supplied.
+
+### Native-committed actions
+
+**Source/confidence:** supplied Steam executable (stamp 1721645006), existing Epic-to-Steam
+map and native action code (high for the checked binary; live behavior unverified).
+Epic Roll start 0x2C7CB0 maps to Steam 0x2C9E60. It sets the rolling flag, requests motion
+0xDC and enables native roll handling. Hook its complete six-byte position-independent
+prologue before any of those operations. Verify its rolling-flag and motion operands at
+runtime before installing. B's Roll is no longer predicted from an earlier command-word
+snapshot: the original native selector proves the ability, input and tilt decision.
+Other actors/styles/scripts and unavailable data forward the original exactly once.
+Accepted B rolls queue one existing moving spin and consume the native start. Explicit
+admission-failure diagnostics distinguish missing data/model/pose from native selection.
+
+Two source-confirmed donor admission restrictions could also leave v14 on native Roll:
+Final may not supply standalone walk/run parameters, and a casting clip can animate both
+weapons without melee hit triggers. Use loaded base Sora movement only if Final's speeds
+are invalid/absent. Fill each missing spin contact from actual ability-free ground basic
+melee metadata, excluding cast/guard/ability/air/finisher rows. Author that missing blade's
+contact over the single spin cycle. Guard and Roll share those exact windows and ATKP
+metadata; no attack ID is guessed. This does not prove either was the user's live cause.
+
+Epic Superglide start 0x2B05C0 maps to Steam 0x2B2750. Run it first to prove native
+eligibility and successful state-21/subtype-1 entry. Verify its subtype operand before
+hooking its complete nine-byte position-independent prologue. In A, leave that native
+state through the existing set-state routine, zero inherited glide velocity and queue the
+real Valor base aerial finisher controller. The actual row retains its root/hop movement,
+timing and weapon contacts. The host starts its finisher slot without fabricated hits,
+Combo Master or another equipped ability. Strip donor events, defensive and combo/follow-up
+windows; native impact/audio/trails still follow its real attack. This is one action per
+native Superglide press; release Square to rearm. End/interruption restores native falling
+at the actual resulting position. An old native glide header is accepted for that specific
+fall handoff, never for a new script/damage action. The v14 cosmetic finisher loop is removed.
+Unavailable finisher data retains the native held Superglide fallback; A regular Glide is
+unchanged. Native attack-ability lane priority remains for ordinary combos.
+
+### Real KH2 spell effect resources, native gameplay retained
+
+**Source/confidence:** existing kh2-magic MAG/BDX engine, kh2-fx PAX implementation, fx12
+D3D12 renderer and native cast observer (high for source integration/portable tests; current
+game rendering unverified). A separate dual_magic_fx runtime loads the actual three levels
+of Fire, Blizzard, Thunder and Cure from the user's KH2 install, plus texcommon.dpd. It
+uses their real scripts/effect libraries at Final's magic subs 30/32/34. It does not load
+or initialize the full overhaul's Reflect, Drive, menu, gauge, stat or magic gameplay hooks.
+
+Only a proven native cast, its current binding and exact NativeCast clock can start a
+visual script. Read levels with the real initialized game module base and checked native
+spell/save addresses; never call Reflect's uninitialized BASE helper. The original Final
+cast clip's magic-release event releases the visual script, once. A pre-release interruption
+cancels that casting task. Projectiles/effects may finish visually after an accepted release.
+The visual World exposes current Sora/selected target/party positions, bones and floor;
+hitback/motion/party-attack writes are absent and all script Strike/attack outputs are
+ignored. No HP, MP, spell damage, healing, status, inventory or ability is changed. KH1
+continues the original spell. Native spell sounds and original effects therefore remain
+in this first effect test. Gravity/Stop/Aero retain native effects and Final cast visuals.
+This is an actual KH2 resource renderer over native spells, not a KH2 spell-behavior port.
+
+Hook the existing world-model pass (Epic 0x1EADD0 / Steam 0x1ECF30) with its checked
+15-byte position-independent prologue; use only fx12's existing camera/D3D12 support.
+Draw after the native world pass with depth testing and normal state restoration. Bind
+the visual runtime to exact actor/instance/matrices/weapon/generation, clear on changes,
+and hide/retire in menus/scenes/unequip. Read-only snapshots and actual current actor
+translation place effects; old pose roots never move Sora. The script effect loop advances
+only on native physics/time, has 20-second idle lifetime and cast/effect/attack/draw budgets,
+and never writes native spell state. Bound effects follow current bones; script-owned
+unbound effects use the script's positions. Visual projectile collision is the portable
+script approximation; it cannot change native gameplay collision or damage.
+
+`dual_b_spell_fx=on` is the new default. Off disables only this effect layer; casts and
+both style actions retain their existing behavior. No game effect assets ship in the ZIP.
+Readiness, package counts/warnings, accepted visual casts and retirement are logged.
+Partial/missing packages retain native spells. A's spells and all non-B spells stay native.
+
+### Verification
+
+Native checks against the supplied executable cover the three prologues, Roll's flag and
+motion operands, Superglide's subtype operand and whole-instruction trampoline lengths.
+The receipt records only addresses/booleans/hash, no game bytes or disassembly.
