+# Four Styles v16: passive single-weapon donors and native spell drawing
+
+**Source/confidence:** the user's v15 report confirms A's real finisher and the KH2
+spell layer; it also reports that B still rolls. The exact remaining runtime gate
+cannot be established without that run's log. v16 replaces the delayed synthetic
+Square entry with an explicit host action, removes the obsolete sampled-motion
+admission for a native-committed Roll, and logs entry, admission and execution
+separately. Native selection still proves Dodge Roll ability/input, tilt, water,
+control and action eligibility. The explicit action path follows the already
+confirmed A finisher approach. Source integration/portable tests: high; live v16
+appearance/input: unverified. A's action and geometry are retained.
+
+The four saved style IDs are 126 Dual A, 125 Dual B, 124 Single A and 123 Single B.
+Only the new entries are appended, disabled, with zero AP. Enabling any style
+disables the previous one in place. All native entries, order and ability policy
+remain. Single styles have one currently equipped KH1 weapon: no offhand loader,
+draw, trail, contact or resource-readiness dependency. Test isolation affects only
+Dual styles. Unequip/rebind retires the same controller, cast and pose generation.
+
+Single A loads Limit's matching one-weapon animation/attack data. Single B loads
+Wisdom's, including base shooting tracks. Both get the existing native-phase
+movement, item, damage, jump, ledge and scene-idle mapping. Missing exact matches
+retain native poses. No general event gesture, swim/flight or unrelated action is
+mapped by a guessed motion ID. Donor selection is explicit and does not identify
+a Single style as an active Drive form; full Limit/Wisdom command policy stays off. Normal Limit magic is absent as a command in KH2;
+missing or non-cast Limit slots receive only compatible base Sora tracks with a
+real MagicCast event. Native KH1 spells still execute. Single A's Glide keeps the
+native held-weapon pose as A does; Superglide triggers one actual ability-free
+Limit aerial finisher through the same native gate, with native fall handoff.
+
+Single B's native-selected Roll starts the actual Wisdom QuickRun/QuickRunEnd
+controller state. Its loaded growth parameters are local to that one action and
+never appear in Character.abilities or the save. Release ends the dash normally.
+Only the active Quick Run state extends ownership; idle/run cannot remain owned.
+Single A's native Guard and Roll get matching Limit visual slots when available.
+Equipped native attack abilities retain their whole combo lane as in Dual A.
+
+Wisdom shots retain only real Effect triggers from base attack clips. Its model
+BDX/PAX is run in the isolated renderer, with no Drive arrival/aura initiation.
+An actor-bound native-contact Strikes instance resolves only Wisdom script attack
+shapes against native eligible hurt parts, with ATKP power/re-hit bookkeeping and
+native feedback. No direct HP write is added. It advances on native physics,
+continues released shots after the attack, and clears on binding/style change.
+Script Strike/heal events from the four visual-only spell packages are ignored.
+Both B styles use those four packages at their correct Final/Wisdom subs (30/10
+plus native level offsets); native KH1 spell damage, healing, MP and levels remain.
+
+**Native visual filter evidence:** the supplied Steam executable's native effect
+VM has an explicit second argument that gates draw callbacks while the unconditional
+update callbacks and time bookkeeping continue. The existing offscreen/hidden
+path calls that VM with zero. The new hook forwards the VM exactly once with zero
+only for matching owned spell effects, preserving its result. The effect constructor
+always runs first and receives its real native record. Resource identity comes
+from the native loaded spell file's effect section, as its loader computes it;
+parent ownership uses the native effect record. Native object sequence and exact
+actor/weapon/room generation prevent pool reuse from inheriting a tag. A bounded
+lease also requires the same native cast ID to have successfully started its
+KH2 visual script; loaded files alone cannot hide a new unadmitted cast. A script
+error or runtime retirement restores native drawing. A scoped
+native spell call/physics context and already attributed parent VM propagate tags
+to unbound child visuals without hiding companion spells. Native resources and
+effect fields are never written. Gravity/Stop/Aero have no matching imported
+package and remain visible. Missing packages, unknown ownership or hook mismatch
+keep native drawing. Only checked Steam hook addresses are installed.
+
+The new native render filter and additional donor coverage require the user's
+in-game test. Portable tests cannot establish actual GPU output, installed donor
+availability or every native effect creation route. Targeted diagnostics identify
+native Roll entry/admission/action, donor readiness, shot triggers/contact and
+native spell draws filtered; they do not label captured damage as finalized HP loss.
