+## Stage 356: five passive styles and native spell ownership (v17)
+
+Source: the user's v16 report (Single B Quick Run works; Dual B still rolls; KH1
+spell visuals overlap KH2), the existing KH2 data loaders/controller, and private
+inspection of the supplied Steam executable (stamp 1721645006, SHA-256
+`d790746245d26159f3ee0e1060e33b2fa2de06941850a4ac724f598722884bac`). No current v16
+log or recording was available. No game assets or dumps are included in source or
+in the deliverable. The rules below distinguish static findings from live behavior.
+
+Single A selects the already-loaded ordinary KH2 Sora rig, character and battle
+records. Its ability-free ground/air selector includes conditional rows, with one
+physical Keyblade, matching passive visual donors and the actual base Sora aerial
+finisher on Superglide. Limit is no longer loaded for this style. Existing KH1
+attack abilities still keep their native lane, preserving the earlier requirement.
+Confidence: high for data selection and controller regression tests; retargeting
+and native timing still require the game.
+
+Style: Anti uses ID 122, 0 AP, initially disabled. All five entries are exclusive:
+enabling another disables the previous one in place. Native ability bytes, order
+and AP remain unchanged. Anti's intrinsic ability-free rows include conditional
+base rows, ground hops and explicit Square rows 11/12 when present. Actual body
+hitboxes (weapon 0), root/hop/no-gravity/invulnerability windows and PAX Effect events
+remain. Keyblade/guard hitboxes, spell, offered-command and script-range behavior
+are excluded. Its real body rig and battle data feed native contacts. Square uses
+Anti Glide and combo Side Spin without granting Guard/Roll. The field Keyblade is
+hidden for its draw and restored afterwards. Sora retains his normal model/colour,
+stats, partners and saved weapon; no Drive state, outfit, gauge or bonus ability.
+Native weapon ability lanes intentionally yield to Anti's weaponless base selector.
+
+Matching native movement, damage, jump/fall/landing and ledge poses use Anti data.
+The upper ankle is aligned below the current native ledge hand midpoint, using the
+actual model up vector and a bounded translation. Native glides can sample the
+loaded Anti Glide row cosmetically. Native locomotion/collision/ability gates stay
+in control outside attacks. Confidence: high for routing and finite body-contact
+controller tests; exact pose/ledge coverage and feel are not tested live.
+
+Anti's Magic, Item, Summon and physical special commands are rejected in menu
+availability, entry/target-parent/shortcut selection and command dispatch before
+cost or item consumption. Field context actions remain usable. Anti's original PAX
+joins the same isolated renderer/texture upload; body anchors, motion-end flags,
+scope/pause/lifetime/vertex budgets apply. These visuals add no spell damage. The
+successful Single B Quick Run and Dual A finisher paths are retained.
+
+Dual B previously required duplicate-resource readiness for a committed dodge. Its
+spin adapter could also fail when Final's cast clip had no melee metadata and
+strict non-finisher ground rows did not supply both hands. These are concrete
+rejection paths, not a diagnosis confirmed by a current log. v17 seeds missing
+hands from actual ability-free Final attack metadata, including finishers, or from
+base Sora's real weapon metadata deliberately assigned to both physical blades.
+It uses base Sora movement parameters. The committed dodge now starts independently
+of duplicate resource readiness; displayed offhand damage still needs fresh blade
+geometry. Single B's working native input hook is retained. Confidence: high for
+removing these rejection paths and controller tests; a new game test must confirm
+which path caused the user's failure.
+
+The native effect output record +0x18 is NOT a caster: its constructor encodes a
+pointer to effect+0xD5 there (flags). v16's fallback ownership read was incorrect.
+The spell VM also runs later on the scheduler, outside Sora's command/physics scope.
+Steam function 28F5E0 creates scheduled work with encoded caster at work+0x18,
