+# Five Styles v18: Quick Run, target spell visuals and Anti darkness
+
+Current passive styles are Dual A (126/Valor), Dual B (125/Final), Single A
+(124/base KH2 Sora), Single B (123/Wisdom), and Anti (122/unarmed Anti-form).
+They are exclusive and 0 AP; only the Dual styles duplicate the equipped weapon.
+No Drive gauge, outfit, stat bonus, partner removal or growth/action grant is used.
+
+**v18 evidence:** the user reports that Dual B still rolls, Single B Quick Run
+works, and KH1 target effects overlap KH2 magic. No current v17 log was available.
+The older log in Library predates these builds and was not used as new evidence.
+Dual B now uses exactly the successful host Quick Run route: Wisdom body/timing
+motions 203/204 are ported into the Final data donor with both Final idle blade
+tracks. Its growth snapshot stays local to the selected dodge. The Guard remains
+the stationary spin. Single B Run uses a separate .75-rate game-time pose clock;
+its native movement speed, Quick Run, other styles and configurable idle rate stay.
+
+The target spark is created by native hit feedback, after the spell VM. Steam's
+shared attack constructor 2B2DC0 (actor, bit, data) writes encoded owner +34 and
+canonical data +5C; it is called by the existing attack wrappers. The visual spark
+routine 2B4320 (attack, kind, point) creates an effect through 2AE650; the native
+contact routine 2B4060 calls it after creating the hit record, then separately
+plays hit sound. Private inspection verified those operations and signatures.
+v18 records only Sora's exact canonical spell rows and their cast IDs at attack
+birth; a reused slot clears prior identity. An admitted cast's target spark runs
+once in that scope, so its effect constructors and descendants inherit the native
+draw filter. The original constructor, spark, target binding, audio and damage
+remain. Other actors, melee, unknown data, unavailable replacements and unadmitted
+casts use native drawing. No native flags, data, HP or MP are patched.
+
+Anti's own PAX idle/arrival triggers identify looping body-bound effects, which
+start once per style binding. One-shot transformation bursts, weapon anchors and
+motion-specific effects are excluded. The aura can persist while Anti is equipped;
+attack effects retain their own retirement and a bounded lifetime. The same single
+renderer/texture upload, pause, room/actor generation and draw budgets apply.
+Unequip/rebind clears it. Anti Glide row 11 must be retained despite having no hit
+window: its real root, no-gravity and initial invulnerability are established in
+this repository's prior Anti data notes (docs/drive-model.md). v17 had removed it.
+
+Confidence: high for source routing, exact native call/field semantics and the
+426 passing portable tests (27 suites; 125 style tests). A Windows release build,
+PE imports/exports and anchor checks accompany the package. Live Quick Run/blade
+placement, target rendering and the selected darkness elements remain unverified
+until a fresh game run. Fire/Blizzard/Thunder/Cure have KH2 visual resources; the
+three native-only spells retain KH1 visuals. The renderer does not draw framebuffer
+distortion programs; missing/unrecognized aura metadata falls back without guessing
+random effects. Relevant diagnostics are QUICK RUN START, SPELL TARGET FX and
+ANTI DARKNESS AURA DATA/START.
+
+## Historical v16 design (superseded by the stages below)
+
 # Four Styles v16: passive single-weapon donors and native spell drawing
 
 **Source/confidence:** the user's v15 report confirms A's real finisher and the KH2
