+# Five Styles v19: cast/attack handoffs and defensive poses (Stage 358)
+
+The five exclusive 0-AP styles and IDs stay Dual A/126, Dual B/125,
+Single A/124, Single B/123 and Anti/122. Only the Dual styles duplicate
+Sora's equipped weapon. No gauge, outfit, second weapon selection,
+stat bonus, party change or extra ability is introduced.
+
+**Evidence and confidence.** The user's v18 test reports a brief KH1 Fire
+pose after KH2 casts, native combo poses just after landing or accepted
+interrupts, and continued Dual B Dodge Roll. This is current observation;
+no fresh v18 log/recording was supplied. Source inspection establishes the
+old-pose admission gates described below. Their relationship to every
+observed flash is an inference, requiring a fresh game test. Sources are
+this project's native command/control hooks, motion bank loader, KH2 data
+adapters and the user's privately supplied Steam executable (timestamp
+1721645006). No executable, extracted animation, dump or disassembly is
+included. Existing native address mapping and guarded hook originals stay.
+
+## Accepted attacks and pose publication
+
+Native command execution, not raw Attack input, selects a legal KH1 row.
+For the four weapon styles the original native attack-ability lane policy
+still wins before imported entry; Anti retains its intrinsic unarmed rows.
+Previously an accepted row was rejected when the preceding model still
+showed landing slot 11 in state 0, a cast, or another interrupted action.
+The same old-pose rejection existed again in physics and takeover.
+
+An explicit accepted-Attack session now carries that proof through all
+three gates. Ordinary passive pose inspection still cannot start an attack.
+Fresh accepted entry clears the cast overlay, captures native airborne
+velocity, and uses the existing native motion setter to request idle and
+retire the prior action flag, as the existing command-cancel path does.
+The normal controller then starts the imported attack. Ground entry also
+publishes a control pulse and fresh-controller handoff. Established action
+sessions retain input while the retired native pose blocks can-act, only
+on live positive-time physics steps outside the native pause/menu machine.
+Actual scripts/events, special banks, body/binding changes, damage requests,
+movement modes and the 600-callback timeout still retire ownership. A hold
+bit already present at accepted entry may retire with that action; a new
+hold after it clears receives normal script handling. No HP/MP write or
+native ability grant is used. Exact landing/jump/ledge overlays also remain
+eligible during the native action-running/input-lock bit; free locomotion
+still requires native can-act.
+
+Native motion requests contain control bits above their low 16-bit ID.
+Regular-bank descriptor lookup now masks the ID before indexing, while
+retaining descriptor/header matching and special-bank guards. Steam's
+mapped motion setter is 29F980 (Epic logical 29D7F0); the original Roll
+requests 010000DC and uses that setter. These operations are privately
+verified. Actual pose identity still comes from the loaded regular bank,
+never a guessed adjacent slot number.
+
+## Native casts
+
+The exact original cast descriptor replaces the fragile 14..97 slot-range
+check. Native cast start/queue and finite native time still determine the
+KH2 pose, with no donor spell/controller events. At cast completion KH1
+can publish a new request before replacing the sampled header. Hold only
+the last already displayed donor frame for at most eight physics callbacks
+while that exact original cast pointer and descriptor remain visible.
+A new sampled header, binding, accepted Attack, scene or deadline retires
+it immediately. An unconsumed repeat cast cannot inherit the previous pose.
+This bridge runs no spell, audio, effect or attack event. KH1 retains spell
+logic, MP, damage, recovery and native movement. Existing per-cast KH2
+visual admission/target-effect ownership and Anti aura are unchanged.
+
+## Defensive and locomotion changes
+
+Both B styles now mirror the existing native ground Roll predicate in the
+control selector before original native Roll starts: native fresh Square,
+command priority, Guard/Roll bits and native direction threshold, can-act,
+water, shortcut and scene gates. Dual B uses its already ported Wisdom
+203/204 Quick Run through the successful Single B host-action path, with
+both Final idle weapon tracks. The committed Roll hook remains fallback;
+its actual native selection no longer fails merely on an old hold bit.
+Missing data still falls through to native behavior with bounded diagnostics.
+The additional selector marker distinguishes this route in a fresh log.
+
+Anti no longer admits intrinsic row 11 (Anti Glide) in its combat adapter.
+Ground Square instead starts the original native Dodge Roll mover after
+field input eligibility, without granting Dodge Roll/Guard in the save.
+Base KH2 Sora body motions 209 (Roll) and 205 (Glide) and their timing are
+copied at runtime into Anti's compatible zero-weapon rig; no weapon tracks,
+base action row or effect archive is copied. Both native glide variants
+use base Sora 205; movement and glide ability gates remain KH1's. The field
+weapon stays hidden. Anti body attacks, finite combo Side Spin, persistent
+aura, and no-magic/no-items/no-summons policy remain. Native movement for
+Roll, matching donor poses and live visual continuity need game testing.
+
+Single B's existing native Guard overlays base KH2 Sora's real row-11 press
+(motion 173), with native blocking/eligibility. Motion 42 is the repel/hit
+reaction, not the guard press (source: character-core's documented guard
+selector and loaded base moveset). The single right weapon follows the
+base pose. No offhand or Guard ability is added. Other Wisdom poses and
+its .75-rate Run remain as before.
+
+## Validation and limitations
+
+All 432 portable tests pass across 27 suites, including 131 style tests.
+Regressions cover flagged request lookup, accepted attack versus
+old passive slots, native ability priority, menu/frozen-time ownership,
+bounded original-header cast tails/repeat rejection, removed Anti Glide,
+finite Side Spin and Single B's guard-press donor. A Windows x64 cross-build,
+existing/new native-anchor checks, source-scope audit and PE import/export
+checks accompany the ZIP. Validation receipts contain final test counts,
+source and binary hashes. The initial reused Linux incremental test cache
+failed to link; portable checks use a fresh one-unit codegen cache. This is
+a build-environment workaround, not a gameplay code change.
+
+No fresh game or GPU execution was performed. Fire recovery in every
+level/air state, immediate landing/interruption attacks for all five styles,
+Dual B direction/Square, Anti weaponless glide/roll and Single B native
+Guard must be verified in a fresh process. Native attack-ability combos
+remain intentional KH1 lanes, as previously requested. Prior stage notes
+below document historical behavior and are superseded by this stage.
