+# Five Styles v20: repair the v19 first-frame regression (Stage 359)
+
+**Current evidence.** The user supplied a 49.6-second gameplay recording and
+reports that all attacks stopped working, imported magic stopped appearing,
+Dual B still rolled, and Single B acquired a glitching/non-ending Quick Run.
+The recording was inspected locally; it and extracted frames are private
+research, not package content. There is no fresh native v19 log. The available
+older log's metadata predates these versions and is not used as v19 evidence.
+
+## Proven native flag correction
+
+v19 mistakenly treated bit 8 (100 hex) at actor +160 as a special-bank guard.
+It added that rejection to both the shared field-action scope and cast sampling.
+The supplied Steam executable disproves that interpretation: its ordinary
+animation update at 29F245 clears bit 8 each update; after consuming a queued
+motion (29F26A/29F277), 29F288 sets bit 8 and 29F28C writes it back. Native
+attack/effect lifetime routines test that same bit as a motion-change notice.
+It is a one-update notification, not a motion-bank selector. These observations
+are primary-source findings with high confidence; the executable SHA and
+anchor results are recorded in validation. No executable/dump is distributed.
+
+A legitimate first frame could therefore discard an accepted attack or clear
+the entire observed cast. The latter also prevents the same-cast imported
+spell effect from being admitted. The new idle motion requested by v19's
+accepted-Attack handoff also generates this very notification. v19's portable
+tests and matching hook bytes did not exercise that engine phase; their success
+was insufficient evidence for the added runtime gate.
+
+The runtime now shares NativeField eligibility for bound normal ground/air
+states outside actual events/scripts. Its motion-change field is diagnostic;
+that bit is never an eligibility condition. The cast keeps its exact original
+header/request/clock/binding checks, queue wait and bounded visible tail. Actual
+binding mismatches are rejected before actor reads. The old passive-visual
+first-frame blanking check is removed too, so the same notification does not
+show a native pose between two correctly matched imported poses. Known native
+slots/descriptors, exact body binding, event/script guards and native can-act
+for free locomotion remain. No motion-change flag is cleared or patched.
+
+## Return Quick Run to actual native commitment
+
+Remove v19's extra B Roll selector from the pre-control wrapper. Both B styles
+again queue one imported Quick Run only when the original native Roll-start
+hook is called, after native ability, direction, facing and action selection.
+A pending/owned roll session cannot queue a second host press. The two styles
+still use the existing validated host Quick Run adapter: actual Wisdom 203/204,
+loaded growth snapshot, release/finite timer, no saved growth grant, and Final
+idle blade tracks only for Dual B. The native original remains fallback when
+binding/data/scene admission fails. No new Roll address or guessed hook is added.
+
+Also remove v19's generic committed-action control override: restore the proven
+native control pulse for the imported step. Accepted Attack and native defensive
+entry already publish their initial pulse. Native menus/freezes retain their
+original control behavior. This restores the path reported working for Single B
+before v19; it removes an extra ordering change, rather than claiming a live
+proof of every prior Dual B failure. Dual B's continued native Roll predates
+v19. Without its current trace, its older cause is not established by the video.
+
+The startup log now records whether the shared native Roll hook installed.
+Bounded Roll-entry lines include style, native state, flags, pending/owned,
+binding, data readiness and hook status. Existing start/failure messages show
+whether the host Quick Run actually began. A fresh game log can distinguish a
+missing hook/data admission from a later controller release; an old log cannot.
+
+## Retained behavior and validation
+
+Keep v19's accepted Attack proof through landing/interrupt poses and native
+attack-ability lane priority. Keep Anti's base KH2 Sora body-only Glide/Roll,
+zero weapon tracks and blocked magic/items/summons; keep Single B's base KH2
+guard press with native blocking. The five IDs, exclusivity/0 AP, Dual-only
+weapon duplicate, A finisher Superglide, cast visual filtering and Anti aura
+remain. No Drive state, gauge, outfit, stat or party changes are introduced.
+
+All 435 portable tests pass across 27 suites, including 134 style tests. New
+cross-feature fixtures cover motion-change notifications with normal/bad field
+scope, accepted ground/air attacks for all five styles, queued first-frame
+casts and same-cast visual leases, and both B Quick Runs held/released through
+end timing and a later independent start. Native update anchors, a source-scope
+audit, Windows x64 release and PE checks accompany this build. These fixtures
+are not live game tests. No new physics, HP, MP, damage or native effect-state
+writes are introduced by this correction.
+
+The scope audit also verifies that the corrected field/visual/cast runtime
+paths cannot contain the discarded +160 rejection, and that pre-control no
+longer queues B Quick Run. Native byte/prologue matching alone does not establish
+semantic behavior. Fresh process verification is required for all attacks, KH2
+magic, Dual B actual dodge, Single B release/completion and map/menu transitions.
+Prior stage notes below are historical and superseded where corrected here.
+
