+# Five Styles v21: native Guard witness, complete Fire and Wisdom dodge (Stage 360)
+
+The user reports Single B showing KH2 Guard only at Fire's end, Dual B
+showing KH1 Fire recovery, and continued Dual B Dodge Roll. No new native
+log was attached. Source/native inspection establishes the Guard/Fire
+identity error; live dodge admission is not established by that report.
+
+## Guard row identity is not a motion identity
+
+The native selector at Steam 2A7C63 passes row 3D to 2A3980 (Epic logical
+2A17F0). That function uses the actor's row table with 20-byte records,
+reads the row's signed motion at +0, and passes THAT motion to the ordinary
+motion setter. Row 3D does not mean motion 3D. Motion 3D is also the native
+Fire follow-up; the old raw-request Guard map therefore overlaid Guard on
+Fire's recovery and did not recognize the actual Guard motion.
+
+Remove that raw map for both single styles. A guarded observer at the
+native row-start entry runs the original once, preserves its return, and
+records a witness only for normal Sora's actual row-3D start in Single A/B.
+The original's before/after motion request resolves the real Guard motion.
+The visual requires that exact actor/weapon/room generation, state 0,
+resolved current request and matching sampled regular-bank header. Pending
+publication has six callbacks to settle; the witness has a 180-callback
+ceiling and is retired on interruption/rebind/scene. A new observed cast
+clears it. Single B and Single A use base KH2 Sora's actual guard-press row
+(motion 173 fallback), retaining all native Guard context, blocking,
+eligibility, effects and audio. Nothing grants Guard in the save.
+
+The new paired row-start address was already documented in combat.rs's
+native investigation. The Steam original and selector call are verified
+against the supplied executable; the five-byte prologue is one complete
+position-independent instruction. The Epic logical site uses the same
+expected prologue and fails closed if it differs. Existing hooks remain.
+
+## Fire has two authored native phases
+
+Private Steam inspection confirms ground Fire requests 36 then appends
+3D; aerial Fire requests 83 then appends 8A. These are explicit native
+sequences (2A3EB2/2A3EBF/2A3EC7 and 2A4221/2A422E/2A4236), not guessed
+neighboring slots. The prior cast sampler retired on the second motion,
+exposing KH1's recovery (or the wrong single-style Guard map).
+
+Only an observed Fire with initial 36/83 may link its respective follow-up.
+The loaded regular MSET supplies both durations and FPS. One monotonic KH2
+cast timeline covers both phases in seconds, clamping each phase at its
+authored end. A phase change requires the already sampled initial phase,
+the exact authorized follow-up, a changed sampled pointer and its matching
+header. If the new id publishes before its model header, the existing
+bounded old-header tail holds the prior donor sample until that header
+arrives. Other spells/motions cannot enter this chain. Repeats, reversals,
+new actors/generations, scripts/events and deadlines still retire it.
+
+The original requested_at/cast_id is unchanged across recovery. This runs
+no new spell or effect event and never restarts KH2 magic. Native costs,
+damage/healing, targeting, recovery, movement and spell eligibility remain.
+FX/pose release synchronization still needs a fresh game test.
+
+## Use Wisdom directly for Dual B's dodge
+
+Replace the old practice of copying Wisdom clips into Final's general
+combat donor. Build a dedicated data-only dodge profile from Wisdom's rig,
+movement parameters and actual 203/204 clips. Its controller has no combo
+rows, saved growth abilities, spell/shot events or hitboxes. The separately
+loaded valid Quick Run growth snapshot lasts only for the host-selected
+action. Both Final weapon rigs remain, using their idle tracks when present
+and normal bind-pose fallback otherwise; optional weapon animation cannot
+block an otherwise valid dodge.
+
+Dual B's native Roll request now admits this profile independently of
+Final's attack/Guard adapter. The same profile supplies controller, rig
+and draw timing throughout that roll session. It still enters only from
+the original committed native Roll hook, with no pre-control selector.
+Single B's working native-commit route is unchanged. Completion/release,
+body/binding/scene guards, native Dodge Roll eligibility and the existing
+ownership timeout remain. No growth ability, second weapon selection,
+stat bonus or new hit source is introduced. The exact older live reason
+for Dual B's Roll remains unverified without a current trace; this build
+implements the explicitly requested independent Wisdom route and logs
+its admission data/start rather than claiming a live result.
+
+## Validation and retained scope
+
+All 440 portable tests pass across 27 suites, including 139 style tests.
+New fixtures cover Guard witness versus Fire id, both Fire phases/rates,
+header publication lag, repeats/reversals, non-Fire rejection and a
+Wisdom-only dodge with no Final rows/events/grants. The Windows x64 release,
+PE interface, 55 source-scope checks and 12 additional native row/Fire
+anchors pass. Earlier first-frame flag, contact/renderer/spell ownership
+checks remain. No fresh game/GPU execution was performed. Recordings,
+game data, executables and disassembly remain private and are not shipped.
+
+Keep all five style IDs/0 AP/exclusivity, Dual-only equipped-weapon duplicate,
+A finisher Superglide, Anti weaponless base glide/roll and restrictions,
+Single B .75 Run, native attack-ability priority, spell filtering and Anti
+aura. Prior stage notes below are historical and superseded by this stage.
+
