+# Stage 363 — Five Styles v24: native glide attachment and visible Quick Run blades
+
+## Evidence and scope
+
+The user confirms v23's action and Fire behavior works. The supplied 39.55-second
+recording shows Dual A's held offhand relocating/disappearing during native Glide
+turns, then Dual B Quick Run with a colored weapon-shaped outline instead of two
+stable equipped blades. The current kh1-dual-wield(3).log identifies s362/v23;
+it records 40 Dual B Quick Run starts and 28 native put-away calls while Ranged
+is active. The previous logs supplied alongside it are historical, not v24 proof.
+
+Keep v23's native committed Guard/Quick Run selection, finite host timing, consumed
+Fire recovery queue, confirmed Single B Guard and all gameplay behavior. This
+update concerns weapon attachment and appearance. No new animation bank, spell
+combo stage, event package, effect, hit source, native ability or form state.
+
+## Keep Dual B's two real blades out during Quick Run
+
+The host marks a borrowed movement donor as field/outside battle when no Drive
+form is active. That is correct for ordinary Wisdom's one-weapon field movement:
+RigAnim::moves_without_weapon includes Quick Run 203 and end 204. Its visibility
+result previously went directly to native put-away and the primary grip renderer,
+even while a passive Dual style required two visible equipped weapons. The native
+actor then had no weapon mesh in its draw params, so the duplicate could not be
+queued either. The put-away path also requests the existing vanish effect. This
+matches the observed colored outline and the explicit put-away log entries.
+
+During owned Dual actions, force the shared weapon visibility result out; leave
+single/Anti/non-style donor visibility rules unchanged. Both keyblade() and GRIP
+use that same result. Thus a native-committed Dual B Quick Run/end keeps the two
+real equipped models and never requests put-away/vanish for its movement phase.
+Its Wisdom body/controller, Final idle blade tracks, movement, timing, growth
+snapshot and lack of attack contacts are retained. No copied movement pose is
+made into an attack, and no new trail/effect event is enabled.
+
+Passive idle/native held admission previously set only actor bit 4000. Use the
+already-mapped native show-weapon function when that bit is absent, so the weapon
+object's RGBA is restored as well. Steam 2A2E30 (Epic logical 2A0CA0) resolves the
+weapon object, writes RGB FF/FF/FF and alpha 80 for argument 1, then sets bit 4000.
+That same routine is already used by takeover::keyblade. Existing idle-visibility
+restoration remains; no texture, palette or raw color memory is patched. The
+Steam routine's appearance/flag anchors are verified against the supplied exe.
+
+## Attach Dual A's held blade to the current native joint hierarchy
+
+The native fallback previously trusted the published hand-world matrix directly.
+The existing native wrist/hold investigation in pose.rs documents partial blend
+frames where such hand/grip matrices contain an extra actor translation, while
+the body and skinned weapon bones remain elsewhere. The glide draw refresh used
+after the primary queue did reject a distant hand, but the pose-side path could
+still publish an actor-bound pose without that actor-distance check. The recording
+proves the visible failure; it does not contain a trace of the exact bad left-hand
+matrix. The reconstruction below removes that untrusted input rather than
+claiming the video measured a specific matrix value.
+
+For native Dual A glide/fallback Superglide, rebuild the left hand from instance
++1B8 (the current parent-local matrices), using the actual body root at +1B4[0].
+The local table is never written by this mod. Root world already contains local
+bone 0, so skip local 0 and compose only descendants through the captured native
+parent hierarchy. This follows the existing native FK convention checked by
+pose.rs's root/local chain comparison. Reject cycles, missing parents and invalid
+or singular matrices. Do not feed the previous duplicate or published helper
+hand world back into the result.
+
+When a fresh binding has no admitted held template, rebuild its right hand and
+13 primary weapon joints through the same local hierarchy before calibrating the
+left grip. Once calibrated, rebuild only the live left hand. The template stores
+weapon-to-hand local transforms, never an old room's world coordinates. Native
+attachment publication now validates hand-to-actor distance on both pose and draw
+paths, and only a successfully published pose increments its admission serial.
+
+At the exact native body draw, clear the prior glide duplicate, rebuild from that
+body's root/local hierarchy, and publish the attachment BEFORE the original body
+queue copies its matrices. The second queue uses this snapshot; it no longer
+resamples after the primary queue. Unknown/rejected geometry stays absent rather
+than drawing a stale or remote blade. Binding, actor/instance/matrix identity,
+scene/script, state, ownership and current-frame guards remain. This rebuild
+reads native geometry into a private vector and only supplies the duplicate; it
+never changes Sora's native body/world/local matrices, movement, trails or damage.
+The owned Valor finisher Superglide bypasses this native-only path.
+
+## Validation and live limits
+
+449 tests pass across 27 suites, including 147 style tests and v23's real Win64
+bridge execution test. New fixtures rebuild a held blade through 80 translated/
+turning native roots while ignoring a deliberately double-translated helper
+world and an already-applied local root 0; reject broken hierarchies/matrices;
+and run actual host Quick Run/end to completion under its real field-stow
+classification while requiring Dual visibility. Existing scene/binding retirement,
+no passive Dual A glide contacts, Quick Run hold/release/timing and gameplay
+regressions remain. Windows x64 release, PE interface, eight native appearance
+anchors and 80 source-scope checks pass. ZIP and saved-copy hashes/CRC/extraction
+are verified. No fresh v24 game/GPU rendering test was performed.
+
+First live test: equip Dual A, Glide straight and turn both directions repeatedly,
+including after landing and a map change. Verify the duplicate stays in the palm.
+Then Dual B Quick Run outside battle: tap, hold/release and repeat in different
+directions, checking two normal textured copies through the end. Check one native
+Guard and Fire cast afterward; retain their confirmed v23 behavior.
+
+All five exclusive 0-AP styles, equipped-weapon duplication only in Dual styles,
+native attack-ability priority, A finisher Superglide, Single B .75 Run and Guard,
+Anti movement/restrictions/aura, spell effects/filtering, native stats and party
+remain. No gauge, outfit, extra ability or second weapon selection is introduced.
+Earlier stage notes follow as history.
+
