+# Stage 364 — Five Styles v25: standard Glide follows the drawn palm
+
+## Evidence and scope
+
+The user reports that v24 fixed Dual B, but Dual A's STANDARD Glide still loses
+or relocates its offhand on turns. The actual Superglide/attack finisher is good
+and must remain so. No new v24 log was attached with this report. The latest
+available numbered log is s362/v23 and is historical evidence only. The earlier
+video shows the symptom but does not measure which v24 matrix was bad.
+
+This revision changes only the cosmetic attachment and duplicate visibility of
+Dual A's native regular Glide. No animation replacement, movement, contact window,
+trail rule, spell, ability, combo, Drive state or finisher timing changes. Dual B's
+confirmed v24 behavior stays intact.
+
+## Use a matrix that the body actually renders
+
+Source: private user-owned Sora model skeleton metadata, the existing MDLS parser,
+and the native queue behavior documented in docs/kh1-weapon-second.md section 2.
+Confidence: high for the flags and native palette behavior; the association with
+the observed v24 failure is an inference pending a fresh game test.
+
+The native queue copies bone 0 and bones whose links word has skin bits 30..31
+set to 1. The hand helper 206 is not skinned. Palm 218 is skinned, has zero local
+translation at its base, and descends from hand 206 through helper 217. Its right
+counterpart is 114. Primary blade/chain bones 282..291 are skinned; grip helpers
+280, 281 and 292 are not. Existing pose.rs wrist notes independently show that
+unskinned helper worlds can contain an extra actor translation in partial blends.
+v24's root/local reconstruction failed the user's live test. Do not rely on that
+reconstruction or interpret a plausible helper matrix as a fresh body matrix.
+
+At the exact Sora body queue, before the original queue copies its palette,
+verify the model's live skin flag and follow world[218]. This is the palm used
+by that body draw. Store only weapon-to-palm local transforms for the current
+actor/model/matrix/weapon/style generation. Prefer calibration from an admitted
+held Valor idle pose. If Glide is the first pose after admission, mirror the
+current skinned primary blade relative to skinned right palm 114, using bind
+orientation only; build unskinned grip helpers from bind data. Never copy raw
+unskinned helper worlds. Once calibrated, no pose-state lock or primary weapon
+matrix is needed to place the duplicate in each draw.
+
+Reject missing/invalid/singular/off-actor skin matrices and mismatched bindings;
+clear the previous duplicate before the draw so rejection cannot reuse a remote
+blade. The hand-local template survives ordinary pose ticks but retires on the
+existing binding lifecycle. The next admitted draw stamps the current frame.
+New bounded DUAL A STANDARD GLIDE notes report the exact template source or
+rejection reason and whether native weapon params were present.
+
+## Keep standard Glide visible without changing Superglide
+
+Source: existing native Glide state/work subtype convention and the native
+show-weapon appearance anchors checked for v24; confidence high for the gate,
+new private duplicate rendering still requires live validation.
+
+The new path requires Dual A, !owned, state 21, player work bit 0 clear, and no
+scene/script/native hold. Unknown work is rejected. Ordinary actor action flag 4
+alone does not hide the cosmetic weapon. Work bit 0 set (Superglide) and every
+owned attack finisher are excluded. The broader native_held_glide body policy is
+unchanged; the owned Valor Superglide uses its existing real finisher path.
+
+Only for an admitted regular-Glide duplicate, allow its queue even when native
+primary weapon params are absent, and reset only the duplicate's private copied
+weapon RGBA to normal FF/FF/FF/80. This is the color/alpha used by native show-
+weapon. Keep original body tint, light and texture parameters. Native actor,
+weapon object, primary params and the primary/body draw are not rewritten.
+The existing temporary duplicate palette substitution is restored as before.
+No new renderer hook is installed and no new passive hitbox is admitted.
+
+The v24 files dual_actions.rs and takeover.rs are byte-identical, preserving the
+actual Superglide finisher start, donor attack data/controller and fixed Dual B
+Quick Run/end visibility. Spell observers/effects, combat and glide movement
+helpers are also byte-identical. The Dual B donor loader and owned_weapon_out
+policy are compared directly with v24; only version labels change in dual.rs.
+
+## Validation and live limits
+
+450 portable tests across 27 suites include 148 style tests and the actual Win64
+Guard bridge execution regression. The replacement fixtures follow the rendered
+palm through 80 translated/turning draws while helper 206 and local root data are
+invalid, calibrate first Glide using only skinned primary/palm data, and reject
+bad skin matrices/bindings. The real runtime predicate is tested against all
+styles, Superglide, owned actions, unknown work, scenes/scripts and hold state.
+v24's Quick Run/end lifecycle and gameplay regressions remain unchanged.
+
+Windows x64 release, PE interface, native appearance anchors, model metadata and
+source-preservation/scope audits pass. ZIP CRC/extraction and saved-copy entry
+hashes are checked before delivery. No live v25 game/GPU rendering was performed;
+these tests do not establish that the visual symptom has resolved. Test regular
+Glide straight and turning, land/repeat and change map, then check the already
+working Superglide finisher and Dual B Quick Run remain correct.
+
+---
+
