+# Stage 365 — Six Styles v26: matched Glide colors and playable dual Roxas
+
+## Current evidence and scope
+
+The new 12.54-second recording shows v25's Dual A regular-Glide offhand stays in
+the hand through the turns, but appears pale/white compared with the primary.
+The user reports it remains still now and has an odd color. Preserve that stable
+skinned-palm attachment. The v25 private duplicate unconditionally replaced its
+weapon RGBA with FF/FF/FF/80. Remove that override rather than changing the pose
+again. Its association with the recorded color difference is an inference; there
+is no new game log with the original per-draw RGBA to prove the exact color path.
+
+The other requested feature is Style: Dual C using the PLAYABLE prologue Roxas
+who carries two Keyblades. Add a sixth exclusive passive ability, not a Drive
+form, boss move package, costume or pair of fixed Oathkeeper/Oblivion meshes.
+The working Dual A actual Superglide finisher and Dual B Quick Run/Fire paths
+must remain intact. No new ability rewards, stats, gauge or second weapon choice.
+
+## Match the native weapon's draw colors
+
+Source: new recording, v25 source, and native draw/color structure documented in
+docs/kh1-weapon-second.md and docs/kh1-tint.md. Confidence high for code flow and
+the parameter copy; the visual correction is pending a fresh game test.
+
+For a native-held Glide duplicate, copy all eight current primary color bytes
+from params +20..27 whenever that draw has a primary weapon. Do not force an RGB
+or alpha value. This preserves its exact native color, lighting/tint contribution
+and fade behavior. If native params omit the weapon, use only this binding's last
+visible held weapon RGBA captured in normal idle/movement, plus this draw's body
+RGBA (+0C) for current lighting. Unknown palette or changed actor/model/weapon/
+style generation is rejected; do not invent white or reuse another room's palette.
+Only private copied duplicate parameters are changed. Keep textures, light
+callbacks and geometry. B and A's owned Superglide finisher never enter this path.
+New bounded HELD GLIDE COLORS diagnostics record current-primary presence and the
+body/weapon bytes, so a remaining symptom can be traced rather than guessed.
+
+Dual C has no special Superglide attack. Its native Glide and Superglide keep
+KH1 movement/body with the same held-palm cosmetic attachment. Dual A still
+admits only regular work subtype 0; its subtype 1/owned finisher remains excluded.
+There are no passive contacts or trails added to either native held Glide.
+
+## Resolve the real playable Roxas donor
+
+Sources: OpenKH object dictionary (object 803, P_EX110_BTLF) at
+https://openkh.dev/kh2/dictionary/obj.html and object structure at
+https://openkh.dev/kh2/file/type/00objentry.html. The latter documents Animation
+Name +28, NeoMoveset +4E, PLAYER type 0 and native Roxas Dual-Wield form 0A.
+Confidence high for identity/layout. Actual installed Roxas assets and game
+rendering have not been executed in this environment.
+
+The new kh2-data::roxas resolver requires exactly one object 803/P_EX110_BTLF
+with PLAYER type, a valid motion filename and nonzero bounded NeoMoveset. Read
+its own animation file and use its own NeoMoveset to select PTYA, pref and both
+wmst weapon tracks; never guess a Valor table id. Preserve the native form byte
+as donor metadata only. No KH1 or KH2 form state is entered or written. Reject
+boss, NPC, single Roxas, malformed/ambiguous records and unsafe motion names.
+The existing generic Sora/Drive loaders are unchanged apart from exposing their
+internal loader to this data module. Files are read from the user's installed
+KH2 backup/live source using the existing archive policy.
+
+Require two real attached weapon tracks, present body idle/walk/run and authored
+base ground/air motions. Check body anchors/parents used by the existing index
+retarget before admission, allowing different wardrobe-only bone counts. When
+Dual C is selected, rebuild the retarget/secondary rig using Roxas's own bind
+skeleton; switching back restores base Sora's existing retarget. The visible
+model stays KH1 Sora. The attachment uses Roxas's actual weapon joints and a
+separate bind-cache key, not Valor's binding. His weapon motion-set trail ranges
+are loaded by the resolved NeoMoveset; missing trail data uses each weapon's
+existing actual contact-window fallback.
+
+The isolated character adapter retains only ability-free base ground/air weapon
+rows with authored weapon 1/2 hit windows, root travel, timing and combo links.
+Strip model events, scripts, body hitboxes, invulnerability, Guard windows and
+command offers; do not import a boss AI, spell emitter or extra action ability.
+Use the existing finite controller and native Combo Plus/Air Combo Plus policy.
+Native KH1 attack ability lanes retain priority. Do not add B's defensive spin
+or Quick Run to C. Guard, Roll, magic and missing visual slots remain native;
+matching idle, movement, jump/fall/landing, item, damage, ledge and interaction
+poses use the Roxas donor. No Roxas model, texture, fixed weapon or game asset is
+shipped. The existing duplicate mechanism still copies the equipped KH1 weapon.
+
+## Ability and preservation rules
+
+Style: Dual C is ID 121, 0 AP and appended initially disabled without evicting or
+reordering native abilities. Existing IDs 126..122 and their native table bytes
+are retained. The six-way native equip toggle disables any other active custom
+style, with both-direction tests for every pair. Unequip retires the controller,
+geometry, held colors, trails and binding through the existing lifecycle.
+The explicit uninstall option removes these six custom IDs only.
+
+Keep dual_actions.rs, dual_cast.rs, dual_magic_fx.rs, native_spell_fx.rs, combat.rs,
