+# Stage 368 — Six Styles v29: map the separately indexed Roxas rig
+
+## Evidence and correction
+
+The supplied s367/v28 log `kh1-dual-wield(6).log` reads the actual playable
+`P_EX110_BTLF.mset` bank (NeoMoveset 10): 229 bones, 32 motions, 10 combo rows,
+weapon attachments 172/63. Admission then rejects source landmark 4 with a
+normalized geometry error of .3698. `playable dual Roxas=false` and
+`attack_adapter=false` explain the unchanged native attacks. Confidence: high,
+directly logged. The earlier parent/geometry relaxations did not establish a
+correspondence; v28 still measured Sora indices on a different-indexed rig.
+
+## Separate source correspondence
+
+`kh1_data::retarget::SourceLayout` builds a data-only correspondence at load.
+Its reference is the existing Sora retarget layout. The donor's two hand seeds
+come from its real loaded weapon attachments, never hardcoded Roxas offsets.
+Base Sora uses its loaded primary attachment and the existing measured left
+hand 86. Each skeleton's own FK supplies positions, aligned by root and real
+hand span. This is our algorithm, not code ported from another mod/game.
+
+Ordered ancestor paths match the arms and hip/knee/ankle chains. Foot candidates
+must contain the expected heel/toe geometry. Remaining measured landmarks are
+matched within the same already anchored hierarchy branches. Branch points of
+the measured tree are retained, without requiring every Sora-only helper or
+wardrobe node. Distinct measured segments/poles cannot collapse. Optional
+finger-detail branches may remain unmapped and inherit the admitted hand.
+
+Require finite nonsingular FK, valid parent ordering, two separate attachments,
+normalized position error <= .20 of hand span and 17 nondegenerate core frames.
+The .20/foot .12 distance bounds are conservative implementation choices, not
+KH2 constants or a guarantee of semantic equivalence. The map is inferred from
+loaded anatomy; live rendering remains necessary. Confidence: high for the
+algorithm/fixtures; actual installed Roxas correspondence is not yet observed.
+
+Only C calls `Retarget::with_source_layout`: existing KH1 target assignments,
+cloth/rest/grip policies are retained while source part indices, rest frames,
+foot poles and hip ratio use the admitted donor map and bind. Default styles
+still call the unchanged `Retarget::new`. Raw animation channels/body poses,
+weapon hand indices/tracks and collision bones keep their original numbering.
+C uses the existing weapon-only secondary path with an empty body skeleton:
+Sora's numbered hair/hood rules are never applied to Roxas. KH1's native rest
+continues to supply those parts. The inverse follows the same mapped parts.
+
+Admission logs real hand anchors, compact mapped body roles and geometry error;
+resource, authored ground/air row and actual motion checks remain. A rejected
+map leaves C unavailable with the reason, rather than silently using Valor or
+a boss rig. No transform, gauge, costume, stats, abilities or fixed weapons.
+
+## Preservation and validation
+
+The complete confirmed Glide attachment/colors file, ability/combo policy,
+controllers, A's real Superglide finisher, B's Quick Run/Guard/Fire and effects,
+C's filename/profile resolver, original retarget constructor/pose methods and
+secondary/inverse implementations remain unchanged from v28. Only the C
+loader, stored source map and C retarget/secondary construction change, plus
+version labels and this additive map API. No new hooks or contact sources.
+
+Five portable regressions use actual production mapping/retarget paths with
+synthetic humanoid rigs: reordered branches and different bone counts, inserted
+helpers, omitted noncoincident source helpers, missing optional finger detail,
+scaled proportions, moving limbs/head/root, inverse/weapon-only secondary, and
+malformed attachments/hierarchies/singular/nonfinite/collapsed anatomy. They
+compare retargeted KH1 matrix output across differently indexed animated rigs.
+These fixtures contain no extracted game data. All 477 tests across 31 suites
+(151 style tests), Windows x64 release, 164 scope/preservation checks, 11 native
+anchors and 7 protected-model metadata checks pass. No actual Roxas game assets are available in this
+workspace, and no live game/GPU execution is claimed. First live acceptance is
+`DUAL C RIG MAP ADMITTED`, `DONOR LOADED`, `attack_adapter=true`, then idle/run,
+jump and basic ground/aerial combos. Native KH1 attack ability priority and
+missing-slot native fallback deliberately remain.
+
