+# Stage 369 — Seven Styles v30: Dual C Guard and playable Riku Single C
+
+## User result and scope
+
+The user confirms v29 works, then requests KH2 Sora Guard for Dual C and a
+seventh exclusive Single C ability using playable endgame Riku. This is the
+first positive live report for the separately indexed Roxas map. Keep that
+map, resource resolver and base ground/air adapter unchanged. The new build
+has no live game/GPU result yet; Riku assets are not present in this workspace.
+
+## Dual C Guard
+
+Extend the existing committed native Guard row witness (already used by Single
+A/B) to Dual C. It observes row 0x3D after the original native start, records
+its actual motion/header and validates binding, state, frame and current native
+request. Raw request 0x3D remains Fire recovery, never a Guard selector. The
+existing hook site, original call, blocking, ability checks, timing, Guard/Roll
+choice and Win64 bridge remain unchanged. Confidence: high for the existing
+native route and local tests; new C rendering requires a live test.
+
+Visual Guard on C selects base KH2 Sora, resolving its actual Guard action row
+with motion::GUARD_PRESS (173) as fallback, not the repel reaction 42. Because
+Sora and Roxas have different indices, C gets a separate canonical Sora
+retarget for this one visual. It never feeds the Sora Guard body into the
+Roxas body/weapon/contact path or replaces C's normal mapped calibration.
+The final drawn KH1 hand supplies the held duplicate during that Guard, with
+no imported hit windows or effects. A first held-attachment calibration now
+uses the selected Roxas/Valor idle and a separate cache; its rig and raw body
+indices therefore agree. Existing drawn-palm Glide/color code is unchanged.
+
+## Playable Riku profile and one-weapon rig
+
+OpenKH's object dictionary identifies final-battle Riku as 2257/P_EH000_LAST,
+separate from party Riku 2073/P_EH000, RTN 2157 and sidecar 2203. It identifies
+W_EH000 as the Way to Dawn weapon geometry, object 791. Confidence: high for
+these documented identities; native installed metadata/content is read at load.
+Sources (consulted 2026-10-31):
+- https://openkh.dev/kh2/dictionary/obj.html
+- https://openkh.dev/kh2/file/type/00objentry.html
+- https://openkh.dev/kh2/file/type/03system.html
+
+Require the unique exact PLAYER profile and its real NeoMoveset, declared
+animation filename (including shared .mset names), and SKLT attachment row.
+Read WMST weapon motions for that moveset. The existing common loader remains
+byte-identical: only the Riku read closure aliases the body bank and the
+weapon model/collision/skeleton reads to W_EH000. Rendering still uses the
+currently equipped KH1 weapon; no Riku mesh, Way to Dawn model, costume,
+party AI, object script or effect archive is installed. Require exactly one
+real weapon rig with a valid attachment and authored ground/air melee clips.
+Resource/map failures log specific reasons and do not substitute another donor.
+
+A new one-weapon entry point builds Riku's separate body calibration through
+the unchanged, user-confirmed two-anchor body map. Use the free-hand SKLT seed
+when present. Otherwise rank mirrored palm candidates with finger-bearing
+subtrees, then require the complete ordered arm/leg, geometry and 17-frame map.
+A weapon leaf helper may use its nearby finger-bearing palm ancestor for body
+calibration, while its actual WeaponRig attachment remains unchanged. Distance
+bounds (.10/.25 hand span) and candidate limit 16 are our conservative inference
+rules, not KH2 constants. Confidence: validated against synthetic reindexed,
+helper/proportion/missing-palm rigs; actual installed Riku anatomy is pending.
+
+## Ability, actions and preservation
+
+Style: Single C is id 120, 0 AP, initially disabled, appended through the same
+native-preserving ability table and save policy. It is exclusive with all six
+existing styles; only Dual A/B/C duplicate a weapon. Native abilities/order/AP,
+KH1 stat/damage/cost logic and the established attack-ability priority remain.
+Single C's controller retains only authored ability-free base melee rows with
+real primary hit windows. It keeps authored links/timing/root, strips scripts,
+spell/effect/voice events, body/second-weapon contacts, donor Guard/invulnerability
+and offers. Do not treat Riku row 11 as Sora's Guard row: kind/window data decides.
+Only existing native Combo Plus/Air Combo Plus policy is carried into attacks.
+No special commands, growth/extra abilities, gauge or transformation is granted.
+
+Matching idle/movement/jump/fall/land/ledge/item/damage/scene/Roll poses may overlay
+with Riku data. Its optional Guard press uses the same native committed witness
+and its own donor/calibration when present. Missing slots, all KH1 spell casts
+and normal Glide/Superglide stay native; this build does not implement Dark Aura
+or party/limit commands. Primary trail windows use Riku's real WMST, with the
+existing per-contact fallback. Riku secondary motion is weapon-only, without
+Sora's indexed hair/hood rules. Every style change still retires old controller,
+pose, effects/trails and binding state, restoring native behavior on unequip.
+
+Roxas loading, its two-hand map and attack adapter remain byte-identical.
+The complete canonical Retarget implementation, secondary/inverse modules,
+Dual A actual Superglide finisher, B Quick Run/Guard/Fire/magic ownership,
+Glide draw geometry/colors, and controller core are preserved. New code is our
+own Rust using existing internal loaders; no third-party code/assets are ported.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+Regressions cover seven-way exclusivity/disabled installation/removal, C Guard
+selection without Fire/repel confusion, separate production body calibrations,
+Riku ground/air primary-only contact lifetime, row-11 preservation, script and
+ability stripping, exact final-player profile/shared motion names, rejected
+NPC/party/boss/unsafe paths, free-hand inference and leaf helpers. Whole-suite,
+Windows release, 164 source/preservation checks, 11 native anchors and seven
+protected-model metadata checks pass. All 488 tests across 31 suites (155 style
+tests) pass. ZIP validation accompanies delivery.
+Offline fixtures do not establish that the actual installed Riku bank/map is
+admitted or that every animation renders correctly. First live acceptance:
+SINGLE C ASSETS READ, SINGLE C RIG MAP ADMITTED, SINGLE C DONOR LOADED, then
+SINGLE C DATA ... attack_adapter=true. Test idle/run/jump and ground/air melee,
+then native abilities, Guard, area changes and unequip. Keep the confirmed Glide
+and Dual A Superglide finisher separate from this new Single C test.
+
