+# Stage 370 — Seven Styles v31: correct Riku data-only profile admission
+
+The supplied s369/v30 `kh1-dual-wield(7).log` reports `final-battle Riku object
+is not PLAYER`, followed by `playable final-battle Riku=false` and
+`attack_adapter=false`. No Riku assets/map were admitted. The same log admits
+the Roxas rig and base adapter. Confidence: high, directly logged. The Riku
+classification is nonzero, but v30 did not print its value; do not claim FRIEND,
+BTLNPC or another specific value from this log alone.
+
+V30 incorrectly treated the controllable final-battle donor as requiring
+native object type zero. OpenKH documents object type, model, animation name,
+NeoMoveset and SKLT as separate fields:
+https://openkh.dev/kh2/file/type/00objentry.html (consulted 2026-10-31).
+Our import reads model skeletons, animation/weapon banks and sanitized combo
+metadata. It does not create a native KH2 object or activate its AI/script,
+control class, form state or abilities. Therefore the class byte is not an
+admission condition for this exact data donor. This supersedes Stage 369's
+requirement that the entry be PLAYER; it does not identify another actor.
+
+Require unique exact 2257/P_EH000_LAST and 791/W_EH000 identities as before;
+classification is informational for both. Never select party/RTN/sidecar/boss
+or Sora substitute profiles. Keep bounded safe filenames, real NeoMoveset,
+actual WMST/SKLT, one weapon/valid attachment, rig/map/core-frame/motion checks
+and authored base melee adapter. Imported animation names still follow the
+selected exact profile's declared/shared bank. No guessed alternate bank,
+table id, attachment, attack row or anatomical mapping is introduced.
+
+Profile retains native type/subtype and prints a compact diagnostic before
+resource reads: exact identity, raw type/subtype, original/resolved motion bank,
+origin, NeoMoveset, SKLT and native form. Bad filename/table errors retain the
+same raw context. After resources read, a once-only, at-most-64-row summary
+prints combo kinds/motions/air flags/abilities/sub-links, motion availability
+and hit-weapon masks before mapping/adapter qualification. These are diagnostic
+reads, not writes or proof of successful HP damage. They identify any later
+rejection without assuming that one has already occurred.
+
+Two new synthetic tests cover the exact Riku identity under nonzero/control
+classifications, metadata retention and invalid bank/table error context;
+existing different-ID/model, party/NPC/sidecar/boss, ambiguity and path/table
+rejections remain. These fixtures are not extracted game records and do not
+establish the installed native type or following asset/rig compatibility.
+All 490 tests across 31 suites (155 style tests), Windows x64 release, 132
+source/preservation checks, 11 native anchors and seven model metadata checks
+pass. ZIP verification accompanies delivery.
+
+All gameplay/ability policy, body calibration/inference, controller/contact,
+Roxas loading/map/combos, Dual C Guard, attachment/Glide/color draw, A's real
+Superglide finisher, B's Quick Run/Guard/Fire/magic paths and other style data
+loaders stay byte-identical to v30. Only Riku data-profile admission and
+bounded diagnostics change, plus version labels. A fresh game process must
+show SINGLE C PROFILE READ, ASSETS READ, RIG MAP ADMITTED, DONOR LOADED and
+attack_adapter=true before imported Riku gameplay can be treated as active.
+No live v31 game/GPU test or actual Riku resource execution is claimed here.
+
