+# Stage 371 — Seven Styles v32: a Riku adapter for the empty PTYA profile
+
+## New runtime evidence
+
+The supplied s370/v31 `kh1-dual-wield(8).log` now reads the actual final-battle
+Riku data: object 2257/P_EH000_LAST, FRIEND type 1/subtype 0, NeoMoveset 65,
+SKLT 19/native form 11, body 209 bones, 29 motions, primary hand 163, no second
+SKLT hand and a 12-bone weapon. The existing one-weapon map passes with free
+palm 53 and maximum hand-span error .1666, producing all 17 core frames.
+Its PTYA set has zero rows. The row-only adapter then rejects ground/air melee
+and discards the entire Form. Confidence: high, directly logged. Rig admission
+alone is not proof of correct live pose rendering, which did not run in v31.
+
+OpenKH documents PTYA as combo-choice metadata separate from MSET motion and
+hit/effect timing, and ATKP as the records referenced by motion hit windows:
+- https://openkh.dev/kh2/file/type/00battle.html
+- https://openkh.dev/kh2/file/anb/mset.html
+Consulted 2026-10-31. The log proves the empty table; it does not establish how
+the original game's Riku script chooses every attack. Do not label our new
+host routing an exact recovered native Riku combo tree.
+
+## Dedicated host melee routing
+
+If the existing authored-row adapter cannot qualify, `riku::prepare_combos`
+constructs host rows from loaded Riku clips and the same loaded rig/ATKP.
+Require a non-movement pose, finite complete root samples, valid clip length,
+real physical strike windows, matching collision shapes and a positive-power
+STR attack record of normal/piercing type. Guard/heal/magic/RC records, explicit
+spell-cast clips and poses available only through ability-gated rows are not
