+# Stage 373 — Seven Styles v34: exact Single C combo, cast and Triangle mapping
+
+## Requested behavior and evidence
+
+User's explicit revision replaces the v33 aerial Square test and combo choices.
+Use ground 152 -> 151 -> 152 (finisher), and air 182 -> 181 -> base KH2 Sora's
+ability-free air finisher. Source identities/durations/contacts for Riku are
+from the admitted s371 log (9); the Sora finisher is resolved from actual PTYA
+rows with air/finisher flags and valid primary-weapon contacts, preferring row
+8 as the existing base-Sora finisher adapter does. The six row ordering and
+follow-up policy are host design. Do not call this recovered Riku AI behavior.
+
+Validate every requested clip before mutating the prepared moveset. Preserve
+real root samples, body/weapon pose Arc identities and hit windows, add input
+continuation after the last contact, and require new input for each step.
+Ground and aerial Combo Plus keep alternating the two base choices before the
+finisher. Native KH1 attack abilities keep their existing lane priority.
+
+Sora's finisher is sampled on its own Sora skeleton, weapon rig and battle
+records under an unused local alias. Remove that alias from the Riku rig so
+it cannot accidentally sample Riku channels. At that step switch RigAnim,
+reset old sweeps and choose the canonical Sora retarget. Other Riku steps keep
+his independently admitted mapping; there is no cross-skeleton interpolation.
+This extends the existing mixed-source fallback mechanism rather than baking
+or relabelling third-party animation channels.
+
+## Input and casting
+
+All v33 airborne Square interception, 193 action adapter, and held Square latch
+are removed. Native Square/Glide and the existing committed ground Quick Run
+remain. Triangle pressed in free normal field plays 195 on ground and 194 in
+air once, through native can-act/deep-water, exact binding, field/script/event
+and menu/shortcut checks. The logical Triangle aliases are documented in
+`docs/kh1-drive.md` (Input) and `docs/kh1-shortcuts.md`; they include keyboard
+and pad routes. Consume only the accepted Triangle bits around the original
+control call and restore them afterward. Reject busy/pending actions rather
+than queueing. These actions contain no donor events, damage/guard windows,
+extra ability, command menu record or automatic continuation; air holds for
+its finite pose then falls. Scripted/menu/context interactions retain their
+normal gates and original native control callback.
+
+Ground Cure/Stop/Aero/Gravity keep item pose 9. Their aerial casts use 193,
+with the existing native cast witness/clock, header retirement, spell logic,
+MP/healing/damage and effect routing. Base Sora Fire/Blizzard/Thunder and
+matching four spell effects remain. Cure's visual release is normalized onto
+193's length in air as item 9's on ground. Gravity/Stop/Aero still have no
+direct base-Sora spell FX counterpart and keep their native effects, as v33.
+
+## Scoped aerial casting defense
+
+The user explicitly requests blocking/parrying/deflection with 193. Prepare a
+finite guard-only copy using actual loaded guard/body shapes, valid bones,
+finite dimensions and real ATKP identity from that source. Enable those guard
+shapes for the visible clip interval [0,length); this full interval is our
+requested policy, not a claim about KH2's original guard window timing.
+All hit windows and effect/script events are absent from this guard copy.
+
+Capture only after the final displayed Sora pose has passed validation and
+been written. The guard witness includes exact binding/generation, cast ID,
+spell, current/previous physics frame and bounded donor-clock agreement. The
+native cast must still be an aerial 193 cast. Reject missing/stale/future draw,
+nonfinite data, implausible displacement, interruption, owned action or changed
+actor/weapon/room/style. Reanchor the captured actual body/weapon pose at the
+current actor and convert native y-down placement to collision y-up.
+
+Reuse `combat::Strikes::guard_step`: native attack objects with priority 100,
+clash type 4, zero power, no damage reaction, body all-round versus weapon
+front-only arcs, bounded real shape radii, regular native rearming/deflection
+and clash feedback. Its existing attack-vs-attack backend is documented above
+in the guard/clash research; no new native hook or hurt/damage interceptor is
+installed. Some native attacks are unguardable; this is a guard, not global
+invulnerability. Whether a specific projectile reflects remains native policy.
+
+A small wrapper initializes native Sora rows and runs only the guard pass,
+not the strike/damage pipeline or any Character step. Explicit retirement frees
+only pool entries still matching the original actor, live flags and this
+runtime's unique private guard-data handle, protecting reused native slots.
+Retain one reusable guard-data allocation across casts instead of leaking a
+new allocation each activation. Checks run before native physics and again
+after native control so ended/interrupted casts retire promptly. Other style
+guards and the existing guard_step implementation remain unchanged.
+
+## Confidence and validation
+
+Synthetic fixtures exercise exact six-slot order, ground/air native combo
+modifiers, no-input termination, source root/contact preservation and distinct
+209-bone Riku versus 237-bone Sora rigs, invalid/missing source rejection,
+finite guard-only 193 geometry, cast/generation retirement, and finite 194/195
+actions with held inputs. Existing Guard/Glide/Fire/Quick Run/native ability
+regressions are retained. All 507 tests/31 suites/161 style tests, Windows x64
+release, 109 source/preservation checks, 11 native anchors and 7 model metadata
