+# Stage 374 — Seven Styles v35: Single C Sora/Riku combo revision
+
+## Requested mapping and source confidence
+
+The user removes the v34 Triangle commands, keeps the other v34 behavior and
+requests ground Riku 152 -> Riku 151 -> KH2 Vicinity Break. Their superseding
+air list is KH2 base Sora first air hit -> KH2 Horizontal Slash -> Riku 182.
+The previous request for Sora's ordinary second air hit is superseded.
+
+Use Sora motion 181 only with a real ability-free, nonfinisher air PTYA row.
+Its standard slot/sequence is checked in `docs/movement-model.md` (Combo
+selection and sequences), also used by the existing hook's sound mapping.
+Resolve Horizontal Slash through actual ability-99 air rows, preferring row
+38; the existing `character-core` Square action map and `growth.rs` agree on
+that identity. Resolve Vicinity Break through actual ability-180 ground rows,
+preferring row 51; checked data/RE are documented below in "Combo rows for
+the foes around him" and the controller's watched-row diagnostics. Require
+valid loaded body poses, finite roots, primary weapon geometry and physical
+ATKP contacts for all six requested sources. Confidence is high for source
+identities and the observed Riku bank; live mixed animation transitions are
+not tested here.
+
+Horizontal Slash is an ordinary Attack continuation in this host combo;
+Vicinity Break is its ground finisher rather than its original surrounded-foe
+opener. These are explicit user policies, not recovered original conditions.
+Only their real pose/root/contact data are used: no new ability equip/grant,
+Square binding, PTYA hop, donor script, spell or command entry. The six host
+rows remain ability-free and input driven. Combo Plus/Air Combo Plus alternate
+the two base steps; native KH1 attack abilities retain their priority.
+
+## Finite 182 tail trim and mixed rigs
+
+The user's admitted s371 log (9) measured Riku 182 at 148 frames with five
+weapon-1/group-1 hits: 17..34, 45..55, 69..77, 82..92 and 108..122. Cut its
+host air-finisher clip by ten frames, to 138 for that bank. Keep the prefix
+root samples through the new end, bound remaining windows, and preserve all
+five hit intervals. Reject an unexpected bank if trimming would remove a hit.
+Keep the original body/weapon pose data and sampling rate: this ends early,
+it does not speed up or rescale the clip. Never mutate the original bank,
+193 cast, Riku's other source clips or any other style. Whether this exact cut
+removes the user's visual drop-off needs a fresh-process game test; ten frames
+is their initial suggested amount, not a measured pose boundary.
+
+Ground finisher and air steps 1/2 have Sora-only aliases on a separate cloned
+Sora rig and battle records. Remove those aliases from Riku body/weapon/field
+pose maps. Select the right rig, collision data and body retarget per actual
+host motion before sampling. Clear old strike sweeps on rig changes and do
+not interpolate foreign skeleton channels. The Riku air finisher returns to
+his separately admitted rig. All six clips qualify before any output mutation;
+missing source data fails closed to native attacks while passive visuals stay.
+
+## Input removal and preservation
+
+Delete the Triangle policy, action-only Character, pending press/session state,
+input interception/masking, native motion setter wrapper and scripted action
+ownership branch. Free Triangle follows existing native behavior again. There
+is no custom 194/195 input binding and no new aerial Square override.
+
+Aerial Cure/Stop/Aero/Gravity remain Riku 193 with the same actual-draw/cast-
+scoped native guard/parry/deflection path. Ground casts remain item 9. Existing
+Sora fallback poses, matching spell FX and committed Wisdom Quick Run remain.
+The cast witness/runtime, native guard/contact backend, cast/FX controllers,
+KH1 spell behavior, seven IDs/exclusivity, other six styles and confirmed
+Glide/colors/Dual A Superglide finisher are unchanged from v34.
+
+## Validation
+
+Synthetic tests cover the superseding six-slot source order, distinct source
+rig/weapon Arc identity and roots, preserved strike windows, input-driven
+Combo Plus/no-input termination, and rejection of missing ability rows, missing
+poses/ATKP, nonfinite roots or a cut crossing a hit before output mutation.
