+# Stage 375 — Seven Styles v36: Single C source admission repair
+
+## Observed failure
+
+The attached local s374 log (10) confirms Riku's exact playable bank, rig map
+and finite 193 cast guard all load. It then reports "base Sora Vicinity Break
+ability-180 clip unavailable", followed by attack_adapter=false, ground_rows=0
+and air_rows=0. Thus rejecting that one requested source disabled both combo
+lanes. This explains the user's default KH1 ground and air attacks. The log
+also shows four native guard objects for an aerial 193 cast; this proves
+object construction, not finalized live projectile/parry behavior.
+
+The v35 source selector passed named Sora attacks through `explicit_clip` /
+`physical`, the intentionally conservative generic Riku melee filter. That
+filter requires Strength scaling and only weapon-1 (or separately qualified
+Riku-hand) contacts. Named KH2 Sora strikes must not be classified as missing
+merely because their actual source uses Magic scaling or real body-based
+attack geometry. Also, its count-99 ATKP lookup differed from the contact
+backend's initial count-0 lookup. Log (10) did not print the rejected record's
+stat/shape details; do not claim which individual predicate failed live.
+The fixture now reproduces the previous rejection for a valid Magic-scaled
+named source; source-specific metadata logs will identify the actual bank.
+
+## Narrow named-source qualification
+
+Keep generic Riku candidate discovery and explicit Riku clip qualification
+byte-identical to v35. Only Sora sources explicitly selected for this combo
+use the new named-strike validator: base air 181, Horizontal Slash from real
+ability-99 air PTYA data, and Vicinity Break from real ability-180 ground data.
+Resolve the same rows, preferred IDs and requested six-slot order as v35.
+
+Require the loaded source pose, finite source root and bounded clip duration.
+For source contact windows, require actual kind-6 body or primary-weapon
+geometry on a valid bone/root, finite positive radius <=1000, finite offsets,
+lift and nonnegative height. Require a real initial-count ATKP with damaging
+kind 0/1, Strength or Magic stat source 0/1 and positive power. Preserve the
+actual record, group, weapon, strike timing and root; do not rewrite damage
+attributes or invent a sphere. Exclude heals, unsupported/secondary weapon
+contacts, guards, invulnerability and all script/spell/effect events.
+
+The existing native contact backend already handles Magic-scaled source rows
+(`MAGIC` derived from actual ATKP stat_source) and real rig body/weapon shapes.
+It is unchanged. These are animation strikes, not an added spell, MP charge,
+FX attack script, ability grant or general Riku-body contact enable. Retain
+body windows in the Character only on aliases qualified for the separate
+Sora rig; unqualified Riku 193 and other body contacts remain excluded. The
+strict original Riku adapter still requires both contexts for its old callers.
+
+## Independent lanes and native ownership
+
+Qualify each three-step lane independently before output mutation. If one
+fails, remove only its host rows and report the exact reason; retain the other
+qualified lane. If both fail, return an error without changing the prepared
+output. Never fill a missing requested slot with a different attack.
+
+The mixed Character may admit one nonempty lane. Before taking a native
+Attack, Single C verifies rows exist for the actual ground/air context (using
+owned airborne state during an existing combo, native state at entry). A
+missing lane keeps native KH1 control. Existing native attack-ability priority
+continues to run first. Each usable lane keeps input-driven base/base/finisher
+ordering and Combo Plus/Air Combo Plus. All source rig, battle and retarget
+selection remains exactly v35; no new input or contact hook is installed.
+
+Bounded startup diagnostics now report Sora 181/193/170 pose, duration, root
+count and contact shape/ATKP kind/stat/power metadata. Successful mapping logs
+both ground_ready and air_ready. A failed lane logs its explicit reason instead
+of silently disabling the other. These run once at load, not every frame.
